144
00:10:06,140 --> 00:10:07,140
There.

145
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:09,140
Now open it up.

146
00:10:10,140 --> 00:10:14,140
This case has slots where you can place three specified slot cards.

147
00:10:14,140 --> 00:10:15,140
But that's not all.

148
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:19,140
You can take all three of them back with you to use in the real world.

149
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:24,140
However, just so you know, you can't take multiple copies of the same card.

150
00:10:24,140 --> 00:10:28,140
You have to choose from one of the specified slot cards there in your binder,

151
00:10:28,140 --> 00:10:30,140
but you can pick any three you like.

152
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:32,140
Hmm.

153
00:10:33,140 --> 00:10:34,140
Okay.

154
00:10:34,140 --> 00:10:37,140
You've reached the end of the game, so you get to make a choice.

155
00:10:37,140 --> 00:10:41,140
You want the normal generic ending, or the one that's just for you.

156
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:43,140
There's one for me?

157
00:10:44,140 --> 00:10:45,140
Yep, that's right.

158
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:46,140
What'll it be?

159
00:10:46,140 --> 00:10:47,140
What'll it be?

160
00:10:47,140 --> 00:10:48,140
Hmm.

161
00:10:49,140 --> 00:10:50,140
I'll take the generic one.

162
00:10:50,140 --> 00:10:51,140
Oh, yeah?

163
00:10:51,140 --> 00:10:52,140
Why that one?

164
00:10:53,140 --> 00:10:55,140
Well, I didn't clear the game all by myself.

165
00:10:56,140 --> 00:10:58,140
And if it's generic, my friends can watch too, right?

166
00:10:59,140 --> 00:11:00,140
Oh, okay.

167
00:11:00,140 --> 00:11:01,140
I see, I see.

168
00:11:01,140 --> 00:11:02,140
Mr. Dune.

169
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:03,140
Huh?

170
00:11:03,140 --> 00:11:05,140
Would you please stop teasing our guest already?

171
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:09,140
I'm sorry, but there's no such thing as an ending tailor just for you.

172
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:11,140
There isn't?

173
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:12,140
Afraid not.

174
00:11:12,140 --> 00:11:16,140
But we were given permission to tell you a few things after you'd beaten the game.

175
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:17,140
Huh?

176
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:20,140
How rude of us.

177
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:22,140
We'll introduce ourselves.

178
00:11:22,140 --> 00:11:23,140
My name is List.

179
00:11:23,140 --> 00:11:24,140
This is Dune.

180
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:29,140
And as you probably know by now, both of us are friends with your old man.

181
00:11:30,140 --> 00:11:34,140
This game was created by Gene, along with ten of his friends.

182
00:11:35,140 --> 00:11:41,140
The name Greed Island was only decided upon because it incorporates the first letter of each of their names.

183
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:46,140
Your father was in charge, so we wanted to select a word that began with G.

184
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:48,140
And it wasn't long before we settled on Greed.

185
00:11:49,140 --> 00:11:51,140
Have you met Razor yet?

186
00:11:51,140 --> 00:11:53,140
Well, he's the R, and I'm the L.

187
00:11:53,140 --> 00:12:01,140
The woman who explains the game at the beginning is the twin of the woman you see when leaving the island, Ita and Elena.

188
00:12:01,140 --> 00:12:03,140
Both of their names start with E.

189
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,140
See that?

190
00:12:05,140 --> 00:12:07,140
And then we've got the letter D.

191
00:12:07,140 --> 00:12:08,140
You wanna hear it?

192
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,140
Wanna hear my story?

193
00:12:09,140 --> 00:12:10,140
Well?

194
00:12:10,140 --> 00:12:11,140
Well?

195
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:12,140
Well?

196
00:12:12,140 --> 00:12:13,140
Well?

197
00:12:13,140 --> 00:12:14,140
Yeah, okay.

198
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:15,140
Then pay attention.

199
00:12:16,140 --> 00:12:17,140
Here's the thing.

200
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:19,140
Your father, Gene, is...

201
00:12:20,140 --> 00:12:22,140
Your dad...

202
00:12:22,140 --> 00:12:23,140
It's a huge jerk!

203
00:12:23,140 --> 00:12:24,140
A huge jerk!

204
00:12:24,140 --> 00:12:25,140
A huge jerk!

205
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:29,140
My name is Dune, you got that?

206
00:12:29,140 --> 00:12:31,140
And what do you think the first letter is?

207
00:12:31,140 --> 00:12:32,140
Uh...

208
00:12:32,140 --> 00:12:33,140
Isn't it D?

209
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:35,140
I can't believe it!

210
00:12:35,140 --> 00:12:36,140
You too, huh?

211
00:12:36,140 --> 00:12:37,140
Makes sense, I guess.

212
00:12:37,140 --> 00:12:39,140
I mean, you are Gene's son.

213
00:12:39,140 --> 00:12:42,140
I thought we were talking about the letter D.

214
00:12:42,140 --> 00:12:43,140
It's W, okay?

215
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:44,140
W.

216
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:45,140
W.

217
00:12:45,140 --> 00:12:46,140
D.

218
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:47,140
W.

219
00:12:47,140 --> 00:12:48,140
U.

220
00:12:48,140 --> 00:12:49,140
N.

221
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:50,140
E.

222
00:12:50,140 --> 00:12:51,140
Spells Dune!

223
00:12:51,140 --> 00:12:52,140
And that was my name!

224
00:12:52,140 --> 00:12:54,140
But even my oldest friends in the world thought it started with a D.

225
00:12:54,140 --> 00:12:56,140
How do you like that?

226
00:12:56,140 --> 00:12:59,140
So when we all decided on the name of the game, I was perfectly clear.

227
00:12:59,140 --> 00:13:02,140
My name starts with a W, and that's final.

228
00:13:02,140 --> 00:13:05,140
But what do you think Gene said when I told him that, huh?

229
00:13:05,140 --> 00:13:06,140
Really?

230
00:13:06,140 --> 00:13:08,140
Then just ditch the W.

231
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:12,140
Starting now, your name is D-W-U-N.

232
00:13:12,140 --> 00:13:13,140
Okay, Dune?

233
00:13:16,140 --> 00:13:18,140
Isn't that unbelievable!

234
00:13:18,140 --> 00:13:21,140
He went and changed my name without even asking me about it first,

235
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:24,140
just so he didn't have to change the title of this stupid game.

236
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:27,140
What's even more amazing is that only a minute later,

237
00:13:27,140 --> 00:13:29,140
Gene already had Dune's name legally changed.

238
00:13:29,140 --> 00:13:32,140
And all he needed was a phone and a computer.

239
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:36,140
Worse than that, he took the E off the end because, get this,

240
00:13:36,140 --> 00:13:38,140
