241
00:13:38,140 --> 00:13:41,140
But your luck has gotten much better as a result, hasn't it?

242
00:13:41,140 --> 00:13:43,140
Well, I guess so.

243
00:13:43,140 --> 00:13:45,140
I've never been healthier and I've been eating...

244
00:13:45,140 --> 00:13:46,140
Oh yeah!

245
00:13:46,140 --> 00:13:47,140
Oh yeah!

246
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:48,140
Oh yeah!

247
00:13:48,140 --> 00:13:51,140
Actually I've never been 8X7 years old.

248
00:13:51,140 --> 00:13:53,140
With every day, he would've added up to life.

249
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:59,140
You can get to walk a mountain, and I'll see how he punished AND

250
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,140
LA JANES 127 year old!

251
00:14:00,140 --> 00:14:24,100
Once I pick the three cards I want to keep, they say I'm supposed to go to the harbor.

252
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:26,940
So what about your father? Did they tell you anything?

253
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:31,180
Yeah, but they couldn't tell me where he is right now because they don't know.

254
00:14:31,900 --> 00:14:35,720
I see. Then I guess the game didn't have any clues for you after all.

255
00:14:36,840 --> 00:14:40,200
Well, no surprise since that's what his message said to begin with.

256
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:41,940
Yeah, that's true.

257
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:45,560
So, let's get back to the three cards. Which ones will you take?

258
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:47,980
How about we each pick one and then go from there?

259
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:52,780
I know my pick, Blue Planet! This is still the one I want!

260
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:56,840
I can't wait to hold you snuggly in my arms.

261
00:14:57,320 --> 00:14:59,020
Which one do you want to pick, Killua?

262
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:03,560
I'm still thinking. Have you got one yet, Gon?

263
00:15:03,740 --> 00:15:05,560
Mm-hmm. I think so anyway.

264
00:15:05,640 --> 00:15:07,260
Really? Which one?

265
00:15:07,380 --> 00:15:10,300
Hold on, let me see. This one.

266
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:11,300
Which one?

267
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:15,300
Huh? Wait, why would you choose this one?

268
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:21,360
Hey, I get it. That does make sense. You are only allowed to take specified slot cards.

269
00:15:21,780 --> 00:15:23,440
Yeah. Sounds fun.

270
00:15:24,100 --> 00:15:25,560
So, when did you think of it?

271
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:29,120
Um, as soon as I saw it, actually.

272
00:15:29,980 --> 00:15:32,360
But, this one's not going to be enough.

273
00:15:32,520 --> 00:15:34,300
Right. We'll need this one, too.

274
00:15:34,720 --> 00:15:35,140
What?

275
00:15:35,140 --> 00:15:37,300
I think it'll work. Do you?

276
00:15:37,780 --> 00:15:38,120
Mm-hmm.

277
00:15:38,540 --> 00:15:41,000
Oh, yeah. And this is the only way to pull it off.

278
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:44,240
Wait, what's the only way? What are you two talking about?

279
00:15:44,500 --> 00:15:46,880
You get the Blue Planet. You okay with that?

280
00:15:46,880 --> 00:15:50,340
Tell me what you're talking about right now!

281
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:02,580
Congratulations on clearing the game.

282
00:16:02,580 --> 00:16:08,260
And now, choose three specified slot cards from your binder. Any three that you desire.

283
00:16:10,940 --> 00:16:14,240
You've chosen number two, Strip of Beach.

284
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:16,860
Number 81, Blue Planet.

285
00:16:17,400 --> 00:16:20,320
And number 84, Paladin's Necklace.

286
00:16:20,900 --> 00:16:23,500
Are you positive that these are the three cards you want?

287
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:24,240
Yep!

288
00:16:24,240 --> 00:16:29,500
All right. I will now return your ring. Very nice work.

289
00:16:31,980 --> 00:16:35,480
Thanks a whole lot, Miss... uh... Miss Elena?

290
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:39,700
So you remembered my name. Thank you for that.

291
00:16:41,700 --> 00:16:42,820
Goodbye now.

292
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:53,600
Welcome back.

293
00:16:53,960 --> 00:16:54,420
Thanks.

294
00:16:55,420 --> 00:16:58,920
What do you think? Are we back in the real world now, or what?

295
00:16:59,460 --> 00:17:00,620
I can't tell.

296
00:17:01,080 --> 00:17:03,460
Well, the game was part of the real world, remember?

297
00:17:03,860 --> 00:17:07,280
Hurry up and get your binder out! Let's get this party started!

298
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:08,100
Book!

299
00:17:08,100 --> 00:17:14,540
Dane!

300
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,500
Yay! This is it!

301
00:17:20,580 --> 00:17:22,140
This is the one that I really wanted!

302
00:17:22,600 --> 00:17:25,120
I've been dreaming about you for so long!

303
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:29,880
I've never been happier!

304
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:31,520
Now, what should I name it?

305
00:17:31,820 --> 00:17:32,300
Bluey!

306
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:33,700
Or maybe Planet Eve!

307
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:34,720
Planet?

308
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:36,960
Oh, yes, yes! That's the one!

309
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:44,560
So, what about the ones you two picked? Happy with your decision?

310
00:17:44,920 --> 00:17:47,560
Yeah. We chose the best ones, right?

311
00:17:47,980 --> 00:17:48,160
Oh.

312
00:17:49,340 --> 00:17:50,520
Well, should we do it?

313
00:17:51,080 --> 00:17:51,440
Yeah!

314
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:53,060
And game!

315
00:17:58,180 --> 00:17:59,420
Killua, I'll take it.

316
00:17:59,420 --> 00:18:11,360
Yes! It really worked!

317
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:12,480
It sure did.

318
00:18:13,140 --> 00:18:14,540
Oh, now I get it.

319
00:18:14,540 --> 00:18:21,840
So, you just used Transform to turn a company into a specified slot card, and then you used the Paladin's necklace to revert it!

320
00:18:21,840 --> 00:18:32,800
That was some clever thinking, you guys, but I have to say, I'm surprised you would go to all that trouble for an accompany instead of choosing another specified slot card.

321
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:41,400
Yeah. It's just, if I hadn't been the first to enter the game, then I wouldn't have noticed. So I guess it was a good thing that I was.

322
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:41,960
Huh?

323
00:18:42,560 --> 00:18:44,900
Do you remember when we played Rock, Paper, Scissors?

324
00:18:45,440 --> 00:18:46,440
You mean John Ken?

325
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:47,260
Yeah.

326
00:18:49,360 --> 00:18:52,040
See, I was the first person to enter the game.

327
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:56,600
And while I was standing there waiting for Killua, there was nobody else around.

328
00:18:57,320 --> 00:19:02,600
That means the first person I met in the game should have been the second to show up, Mr. Gorenu.

329
00:19:02,600 --> 00:19:09,900
But he wasn't. When I checked my binder, it said that there was somebody I'd met before him.

330
00:19:12,780 --> 00:19:16,480
Jean is spelled G-I-N-G.

331
00:19:17,260 --> 00:19:20,200
Oh, I see. So Neeg is an anagram.

332
00:19:23,500 --> 00:19:28,120
My guess is that when I was just a baby, I must have come here with Jean.

333
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:33,580
Maybe this was his way of trying to tell me.

334
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:38,620
If I'm ready to give up everything I have and go find him,

335
00:19:39,080 --> 00:19:41,800
then I have to get strong enough to clear the game.

336
00:19:48,760 --> 00:19:51,540
You really are tenacious. It's impressive.

337
00:19:52,460 --> 00:19:55,580
Well, what are you planning to do once you find Jean?

338
00:19:55,580 --> 00:19:58,240
Jean, that's easy. I'll introduce him to Killua.

339
00:19:58,240 --> 00:19:58,620
Huh?

340
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:01,720
I'll tell him he's my best friend in the world.

341
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:03,820
You what?

342
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:04,860
Shut up.

343
00:20:05,260 --> 00:20:06,600
That's embarrassing, man.

344
00:20:09,300 --> 00:20:09,860
Really?

345
00:20:10,120 --> 00:20:10,300
Huh?

346
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:11,880
Oh, stop.

347
00:20:12,580 --> 00:20:12,980
Huh?

348
00:20:17,340 --> 00:20:21,200
I can't take it.

349
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:24,920
It must be my age, but it's so easy to make me cry.

350
00:20:26,740 --> 00:20:30,100
Oh, hey. Why don't you come with us to see Jean, Biscuit?

351
00:20:32,560 --> 00:20:34,900
Thank you, but I think I'll pass.

352
00:20:36,020 --> 00:20:38,160
I'm not interested in men with kids.

353
00:20:40,820 --> 00:20:41,260
Okay.

354
00:20:41,260 --> 00:20:41,340
Okay.

355
00:20:41,340 --> 00:20:49,060
If I stay much longer, I'll get too attached to them. Like a parent.

356
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:53,680
I guess that's it then. Take care, Biscuit.

357
00:20:54,120 --> 00:20:56,320
I will. You boys too, okay?

358
00:20:59,240 --> 00:21:00,800
Thanks so much for everything.

359
00:21:01,720 --> 00:21:02,180
Us!

360
00:21:02,180 --> 00:21:14,640
A company on!

361
00:21:15,860 --> 00:21:16,420
Neg!

362
00:21:30,420 --> 00:21:31,380
Bye, boys.

363
00:21:32,180 --> 00:21:59,060
Goon has cleared the game that his father created, becoming much stronger in the process.

364
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:04,020
Is the one waiting before him really Jean, or is it someone else?

365
00:22:04,020 --> 00:22:05,020
Bye, boys.

